{
  "_about": "Maps the fly phrases fishing reports use to catalog flies. A phrase maps to one or more tokens, and a report row counts as a hit when any fly in our top 5 matches any token. A token is a catalog fly id, food:<id> (flies that imitate that food with weight 0.5 or more), family:<name> (dry, emerger, nymph, wet, streamer, topwater), or a group below. Terms separated by spaces must all match, and a leading ! excludes. Rule for new phrases: use the catalog fly when the pattern is in the catalog (color and bead variants included); else the food it imitates when the report makes that clear; else the fly type when the report only gives a type. Named local patterns whose food or type the report doesn't pin down go under uncataloged and are counted as catalog gaps, not mapped by guesswork.",
